6. Verify the `searchedAt` value is generated per-request via `new Date().toISOString()` (not a module-level constant) so successive requests return distinct ISO-8601 timestamps.

7. Run the existing test suite (e.g., `npm test` or `npx jest`) to confirm all acceptance criteria pass, including: valid `/search` returns 200 with `count === flights.length`; missing required params return 400 JSON; absent `adults` defaults to 1; non-numeric `adults` returns 400; `/cheapest` returns the min-price flight or 404 on empty results; missing required params on `/cheapest` return 400.

8. If any tests fail, fix the implementation in `/home/bradleyjerong/projects/skyscanner-app/src/server.ts` and re-run the suite until all tests pass.
